# `socket[kRequest] = request`, where all that kRequest can be is one symbol that is made once: the access goes by the key of the symbol, and a name that is stored on the objects of a layout that does not list it is a field that Link appends, whether it is a text or a symbol.
# Until then such a store made an extra property of each object: six names a request on the socket and the response of node:http.
# RUN: link fields mechanisms=all
# CHECK: field L0.1 symbol("request")@m0:0 appended
# RUN(STORE): walk f1 mechanisms=all-Inlining
# STORE-LABEL: code f1:Body
# STORE: PutSlotOrAdd {{*}}key=symbol("request")@m0:0 receivers=[L0]
# RUN(READ): walk f2 mechanisms=all-Inlining
# READ-LABEL: code f2:Body
# READ: = GetSlot{{*}}key=symbol("request")@m0:0
